\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Dynamical MLR from this work. \emph  {Panel (a):} mass as a function of $M_G$ at $[\mathrm  {M/H}]=-0.6,-0.3,0,+0.3$ (solid lines, shaded bands: posterior credible intervals), compared with PARSEC at the same metallicities (dashed lines), \citet  {Hwang2024DynamicalMasses} (dash-dotted), and literature masses: eclipsing binaries (Xiong et al. 2023), visual orbits \citep  {Mann2019}, Gaia orbits plus SB2 \citep  {Chevalier2023}, and asteroseismology \citep  {Serenelli2017}. \emph  {Panel (b):} mass relative to PARSEC at $[\mathrm  {M/H}]=0$. The grey band shows the systematic uncertainty from the shape of $p(\setbox \z@ \hbox {\mathsurround \z@ $\textstyle u$}\mathaccent "0365{u})$ at $[\mathrm  {M/H}]=0$.}}{6}{}\protected@file@percent }
